pokemon legends arceus looks incredible  with the game's release fast approaching  now is the perfect time to break down  everything that we do know about the  game if you're excited for this game  like i am then be sure to like this  video and sub to the channel because  we're gonna have a whole lot of pokemon  coming your way  there's so much to talk about so let's  dive right into the story pokemon  legends arceus takes place in the  distant past and what we currently know  as sinnoh except in the game it's known  as the hissui region mount coronet  remains dominant on the region's horizon  and this frontier represents a time when  pokemon inhumans did not live in harmony  our character is part of the galaxy team  survey corps and your goal is to  basically go out on different  assignments and expeditions and observe  pokemon for research don't worry you'll  have plenty of opportunities to train  catch and battle pokemon out in the  field as well along the way you'll  encounter different characters such as  wardens which are basically gym leaders  as well as other pokemon some new some  old with distinct new features though  you'll even run into different clans  representing diamond and pearl  respectively some of the pokemon in the  story have been blessed with mysterious  power and are considered noble pokemon  many noble pokemon have been undergoing  a frenzy due to a strange phenomenon  that isn't quite understood as a member  of the survey corps you will be tasked  with finding a solution and will be  called upon to help the frenzied pokemon  out of their current state overall your  goal is the same as many other games in  the franchise to see every pokemon in  the hisoui region and conduct research  to complete the first ever pokedex it is  worth noting that simply catching  pokemon won't get the job done either  you'll have to go deeper and carry out  various tasks to fully complete a  pokedex entry by observing and  researching all the different pokemon we  also have a whole new cast of characters  to encounter throughout legends arceus  making up different groups and factions  to go alongside the new story of course  our protagonist and our counterpart are  usually pokedex partners friends or  rivals your counterpart will be either  akari or rey depending on which  character that you choose the pokemon  professor in this game is professor  laverton who has conducted research on  pokemon and has the ultimate goal of  completing the world's first pokedex  other members of the galaxy team such as  commander kamado and captain celine are  senior members who hold themselves to  high standards and can be strict then  you have the wardens unlike most people  in the hisou region these characters are  potent trainers who have mastered  training pokemon and are best compared  to gym leaders from the modern games in  legends arceus these wardens have the  vital task of taking care of the noble  pokemon the wardens make sure the  pokemon have food and their territories  are protected mai and east khan are two  examples each taking care of a  particular type of pokemon pokemon  legends arceus is also the home to the  two primary conflicting clans the  diamond and pearl clans each with their  own leader adaman and irida the two  clans don clothing that resembles pretty  familiar pokemon for those who have  played the diamond in pearl games each  clan pays homage and respect to the  special pokemon they refer to as lords  and ladies all of which can be  considered noble pokemon some of the  wardens even have clan allegiances too  for example irizu is part of the diamond  clan while leon's loyalty is with pearl  here's a quick fun fact as we go through  the wide castle characters you can see  physical resemblances between certain  characters from legends arceus and those  in diamond and pearl indicating family  lineage commander kamado for example has  a striking resemblance to professor  rowan also akari and rey they look like  diamond and pros lucas and dawn  the hussui region will be incredibly  diverse with different sections of the  map serving as the habitat for various  species of pokemon some only appearing  in particular areas or during certain  times of the day this region aspect  isn't particularly new to pokemon fans  but it's worth noting that the region  seems to be more open than any pokemon  game to date however game freak has  shied from outright claiming that it's a  genuinely open world game like breath of  the wild instead the game seems to have  more of a monster hunter approach you  start at a central hub such as jubilee  village venture out into the wilderness  and battle survey or catch wild pokemon  then you return to the village or you  set up a camp in the region the galaxy  team calls jupiter village its home and  is the main operations base for the  survey security and medical corps  venture out and you'll see distinct  parts of the map such as the obsidian  field lens among numerous other areas  you can see a variety of landscapes and  locations in the trailers released so  far ranging from the sea to quiet  meadows and dense woods all along the  frontier the different pokemon and  legends arceus is what i'm personally  looking forward to the most we have a  sweet variety of starters right off the  bat each from a different pokemon game  cyndaquil from gen 2 oshawa from gen 5  and rowlet from gen 6. it is not an easy  choice all three starters are excellent  companions and trainers especially new  ones they'll learn to fall in love with  them just like we all did with our first  pokemon game when it comes to what  separates legends arceus and makes it  different from other games it is the  different variations and twists on  pokemon that we're used to seeing  turning them into something brand new  let's start with noble pokemon a  mysterious blessing has been granted to  certain pokemon that distinguishes them  from other standard wild pokemon some  noble pokemon are friendly and willing  to work alongside trainers but others  are far more aggressive and they might  attack on sight it's not entirely clear  why but noble pokemon can go into a  dangerous frenzy that demands the survey  core's attention you also have alpha  pokemon the easiest way to tell which  pokemon is alpha is by simply looking at  their eyes all alpha pokemons seem  larger than average with glowing red  eyes and they are super aggressive  they'll attack you or chase you down on  site however the benefit of catching  them is vast successfully catch an alpha  pokemon and they can become valuable  partners on your team and some may even  drop extra rare items historically when  you catch a lot of pokemon you stash  them away in pc boxes ready to swap in  and out of your battle teams at a  pokemon center this time in legends  arceus there is no pc storage system  instead you'll have your pokemon relax  and roam close off pastures within  jubilate village there are some new  hisoui exclusive evolutions to classic  pokemon as well were deer the normal  psychic deer pokemon is an evolution of  stantler while basculesian and cleaver  are evolutions of basculin and scyther  regional variants of pokemon have been a  thing for a few generations now such as  alolan and golerian forms and the hisui  region has its own set of exclusive  forms one recently revealed his sui form  is voltorb sporting a dope wood finish  volturb has different typing being an  electric grass type pokemon now some  other hissui forms include growlithe  braviary and zoroark then we've got the  mythical pokemon of course arceus  darkrai and shaman have all been  confirmed although we don't have any  idea yet on how exactly we'll be  encountering these pokemon at the moment  darkrai isn't in brilliant diamond and  shining pearl as of its launch so  personally it's exciting to see dark  ryan legends arceus  all right lastly let's talk about the  gameplay there is a level of seamless  transitions apparently between  adventuring and battling which has me  pretty excited the core gameplay loop  when searching for pokemon can be broken  down into four steps seek observe weaken  and catch the world is rich and you  can't expect to see every pokemon simply  emerge from the tall grass since you  might have to take things a step further  and search for pokemon hidden in rock  crevices or tucked away in the branches  of a tree you'll also want to observe a  pokemon's behavior before deciding if  you will battle it as mentioned before  particularly with noble pokemon some of  them might be aggressive which means you  will want to be as stealthy as possible  before engaging if you decide to weaken  a pokemon first you will want to chuck a  pokeball containing one of your pokemon  at your target which will seamlessly  trigger a battle the flow of action will  not be like previous games which were  always turn based this time your pokemon  stats and battle style will determine  the flow allowing some pokemon to attack  several times in a row you could also  potentially mix things up by having your  pokemon launch a few attacks and then  aiding or healing them with a battle  item or some medicine all within the  same turn no hms in this game either  from what i can see instead you have a  unique item known as the celestica flute  which will summon certain hisui pokemon  that will let you traverse the region  through land sea or air fly with the  braviary speed through fields with the  word deer or surf the water with a  basket lesion when battling there are  two notable styles agile and strong  these styles will change the way a move  hits with the agile style raising your  pokemon's action speed but reducing the  strength of each hit strong style means  fewer moves in quick succession but a  more substantial impact for each attack  combined with your opponent's stats  versus your party's built this will go a  long way in dictating how battles play  out throughout your adventure once the  pokemon is weakened you'll have to aim  carefully and toss a pokeball or heavy  ball at your target and if the pokemon  doesn't burst out of the ball then it's  a successful catch when it comes to  battling frenzied pokemon simply  weakening your opponent won't cut it  anymore instead you will have to  actually dodge the frenzy pokemon's  attacks and try to soothe it by throwing  bombs these bombs are made up of the  frenzied pokemon's favorite foods and  the best tactic is to combine throwing  the bombs while weakening the frenzied  pokemon the weaker the pokemon gets the  greater the chance your bombs will be  effective throughout the game you will  also encounter trading posts that will  let you trade the pokemon you've caught  with other players there are even  customization options for your character  namely through the clothing shop and  hairdressers besides customizing  cosmetics you can also scrounge for  materials to use in the new crafting  system it seems like a straightforward  system combining particular materials at  any workbench for items that you can use  in the field such as pokeballs there are  general stores and craft works where you  can replenish your supplies and by  crafting recipes expanding the threshold  of items that you can combine they're  supposed to be pokemon home support for  legends arceus but just not at launch  and there are estimates of the service  will be available in late 2022.  man that's a lot to chew on and this  close to launch there is a lot more that  we'll discover soon be sure to stick  with gamespot because we'll have a  review and a lot of good tips and guides  coming your way we even got a fun things  you didn't know about pokemon video live  right now on our channel so check that  out i really want to know what you guys  are most excited about in the comments  below and if you've already seen the  leaks please keep the comments spoiler  free if you got any other questions make  sure to drop them in there too and sound  off until next time  [Music]
 

